repository-code: "https://github.com/Grkila/gridlab-ev-grid-simulator"
url: "https://github.com/Grkila/gridlab-ev-grid-simulator"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  GridLab simulates electric-vehicle charging on a synthetic Novi Sad power grid
  using OpenStreetMap data and pandapower. The Windows application compares
  charging controllers, electrical constraints, benchmarks, and reinforcement
  learning. It includes a local Codex assistant and Model Context Protocol tools.
  The network is a planning proxy, not an as-built utility model.
  Team Jokić & Grković³ developed the application for the Schneider Electric
  EV Days Challenge hackathon.
keywords:
  - electric vehicles
  - EV charging
  - power grid simulation
  - charging optimization
  - pandapower
  - OpenStreetMap
  - reinforcement learning
  - Model Context Protocol
